                        "sense_id": "fac71f8f-04d6-3271-bc86-e7a16c015233",
                        "entry_id": "dd21cc1a-55ed-390a-9c7c-aa680066f09c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the English writer and lexicographer Samuel Johnson (1709–1784), or characteristic of his style."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "668ac955-727d-4ebc-8c6b-218d4d1f312a",
                                "sense_id": "fac71f8f-04d6-3271-bc86-e7a16c015233",
                                "text": "With my idea of the rector derived from a picture in the dining-parlour, stiff and stately […]—it was strange to read these letters. They were full of eager, passionate ardour; short homely sentences, right fresh from the heart (very different from the grand Latinised, Johnsonian style of the printed sermon preached before some judge at assize time)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d19688be-2b74-4f1e-bb75-720712965806",
                                "sense_id": "fac71f8f-04d6-3271-bc86-e7a16c015233",
                                "text": "Literary Bengali of prose, during the greater part of the 19th century, was thus a doubly artificial language ; and, with its forms belonging to Middle Bengali, and its vocabulary highly Sanskritised, it could only be compared to a ‘ Modern English ’ with a Chaucerian grammar and a super-Johnsonian vocabulary, if such a thing could be conceived."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c3cdb96-0ed1-3b0c-af71-ba69d1f35ae9",
                        "entry_id": "dd21cc1a-55ed-390a-9c7c-aa680066f09c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to Lyndon B. Johnson (1908–1973), American politician and president of the United States from 1963 to 1969."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f6ea5c7-ae70-34b9-912c-8db2eefa9c61",
                        "entry_id": "dd21cc1a-55ed-390a-9c7c-aa680066f09c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to Boris Johnson (born 1964), English politician and prime minister of the United Kingdom from 2019 to 2022."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "087abdd4-9fe0-433c-af1f-2737f1345269",
                                "sense_id": "6f6ea5c7-ae70-34b9-912c-8db2eefa9c61",
                                "text": "To stop no-deal, MPs must adopt some Johnsonian ruthlessness and be ready to bring down the prime minister and put someone else, probably Jeremy Corbyn, in his place."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
